  "solution": {
    "brief": "Wasp collider and containment: collision detection between aggregated parts and boundary geometry to constrain growth within a volume",
    "principle": "\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Tutorial 06 (wasp_06_multi_part) is the direct successor to this tutorial (05). It extends the collider/containment-bounded aggregation workflow established here by introducing: (1) multiple distinct part types with different connection configurations in a single aggregation, and (2) custom attributes on WaspPart definitions for per-part metadata. The spatial boundary constraint system from tutorial 05 remains in place in tutorial 06 — learners should understand collider/containment before engaging with multi-part configuration management and attribute annotation.",
